    "title": "\"If My People\" | Letters | timesnews.net",
    "text": "One of the better ways to heal and move forward is to acknowledge one’s responsibility concerning their circumstances — in other words, admit that they are/were broken. Doing so requires faith, humility, strength and maturity. We, the people, called Americans, have yet to acknowledge the brokenness of slavery.",
